<title>FRANCE: Axa sells 1.25 bln Ffr of Axa bonds.</title>
<headline>Axa sells 1.25 bln Ffr of Axa bonds.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The group controlling French insurer Axa -- Finaxa, ANF and Axa mutual insurance companies -- said on Wednesday it raised 1.25 billion francs through the sale of Axa convertible bonds to help fund the purchase of Axa shares from Italian insurer Generali.</p>
<p>It said it sold on Tuesday 798,751 convertible Axa six percent 1993-2001 bonds at a price of 1,565 francs per share.</p>
<p>The operation allowed Finaxa to make a net capital gain of 36.2 million francs while ANF, a unit of Finaxa, made a net capital gain of 14.6 million francs.</p>
<p>&quot;Revenues from this sale are partly helping to finance the purchase of Axa shares from Generali announced on September 6,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
